{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_adr_019_scenario_kinds_are_conditions", "label": "ADR-019 Scenario kinds are the what-if conditions (impact 1.0.0)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-019-scenario-kinds-are-conditions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_019_scenario_kinds_are_conditions_scenario_kinds", "label": "SCENARIO_KINDS (conditions plus maintenance)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-019-scenario-kinds-are-conditions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One vocabulary: the contract's old failure scopes (component, power, rack, site...) disagreed with the console's conditions (failed, degraded, power_loss...), so every saveScenario failed zod validation. Scope kinds dropped: a scenario's scope is its component list, not a tag; a future scope dimension is an option that expands the list. The console's IMPACT_CONDITIONS is SCENARIO_KINDS."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_019_scenario_kinds_are_conditions_scenario_kind_severity", "label": "SCENARIO_KIND_SEVERITY (Record<ScenarioKind, state>)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-019-scenario-kinds-are-conditions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Maps each kind to down/degraded/at_risk; typed as Record so a new kind without a severity fails to compile; both the console's condition table and the API's severityFor read it."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_019_scenario_kinds_are_conditions_containment_propagation", "label": "Containment propagates for logical containers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-019-scenario-kinds-are-conditions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The traversal never followed contains, so a component failure never reached its application or business service and every scenario reported nothing affected. contains joins GRAPH.impactEdgeTypes, gated on GRAPH.impactContainerTypes (application, k8s_namespace, k8s_cluster) so a switch is never taken down by one of its interfaces; communicates_with stays out because it carries no direction of dependency."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_019_scenario_kinds_are_conditions_validation_errors_say_why", "label": "Validation errors carry zod issues", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-019-scenario-kinds-are-conditions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "parseInput puts the zod issues in the message so a client sees 'invalid ScenarioInput: kind: Invalid option' instead of a bare label; the generic 'Something went wrong' had hidden the server's reason and the unit test stubbed the API so could not see the disagreement."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_019_scenario_kinds_are_conditions_impact_contract_1_0_0", "label": "Impact contract 1.0.0 (major bump, migration 0012/0013)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-019-scenario-kinds-are-conditions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Enum members removed, so a major bump per CONTRACTS.md; Postgres enum ScenarioKind recreated with power->power_loss, network->link_down, else failed; runbook column added because every scenario read failed its parse without it."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_019_scenario_kinds_are_conditions_graph_impact_edge_types", "label": "GRAPH.impactEdgeTypes / GRAPH.impactContainerTypes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-019-scenario-kinds-are-conditions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_019_scenario_kinds_are_conditions_t_122", "label": "T-122 end-to-end wh